1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,217
One bad line can

2
00:00:01,217 --> 00:00:02,727
crash your whole program!

3
00:00:02,947 --> 00:00:04,071
This is Go Part

4
00:00:04,071 --> 00:00:05,719
30, panic and recover.

5
00:00:06,439 --> 00:00:07,674
The slice has three

6
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:08,778
items, but we ask

7
00:00:08,778 --> 00:00:09,753
for index five.

8
00:00:09,973 --> 00:00:11,916
Go panics, the program stops,

9
00:00:11,916 --> 00:00:13,323
and end never prints.

10
00:00:14,043 --> 00:00:15,436
To catch a panic, put

11
00:00:15,436 --> 00:00:17,757
recover inside a deferred function.

12
00:00:17,977 --> 00:00:20,215
If something panics, recover grabs

13
00:00:20,215 --> 00:00:21,399
it, and we turn it

14
00:00:21,399 --> 00:00:22,715
into a normal error.

15
00:00:23,435 --> 00:00:24,439
Ten divided by

16
00:00:24,439 --> 00:00:25,515
two gives five.

17
00:00:25,735 --> 00:00:27,670
Ten divided by zero panics,

18
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:29,534
but recover catches it and

19
00:00:29,534 --> 00:00:30,752
returns an error.

20
00:00:30,972 --> 00:00:32,494
And the program keeps running!

21
00:00:33,214 --> 00:00:34,787
Next time, goroutines.

22
00:00:35,007 --> 00:00:36,064
Quick one: for a

23
00:00:36,064 --> 00:00:37,650
normal bad input, return

24
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:38,839
an error or panic?

25
00:00:39,059 --> 00:00:39,990
Pick one in the

26
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:42,224
comments, and follow CareerWithCode!

